sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Owner as Vehicle Owner (MEMBER/USER)
    participant App as Web/Mobile App
    participant Chat as Chatbot API
    participant LLM as LLM (Ollama Qwen2.5/Llama 3.1)
    participant Tool as Tool Executor
    participant API as Tenant-scoped Backend API
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Owner->>App: "Where is my car?"
    App->>Chat: POST /api/v1/chatbot/message\n{tenantId (from JWT), text}
    Chat->>LLM: prompt + available tools\n(getVehicleLocation, getHistory,\ngetSnapshot, getParkingStatus)
    LLM-->>Chat: tool_call getVehicleLocation(licensePlate?)
    Chat->>Tool: execute getVehicleLocation()
    Tool->>API: GET /api/v1/vehicles/{plate}/location\n(tenant_id enforced from caller's JWT)
    API->>DB: SELECT Vehicle.current_slot_id,\nParkingSlot.code, Site.name\nWHERE tenant_id = :tenant_id
    DB-->>API: slot=A02, site="Downtown Lot"
    API-->>Tool: {slot: "A02", site: "Downtown Lot",\nlastSeenAt}
    Tool-->>Chat: tool result
    Chat->>LLM: tool result appended to context
    LLM-->>Chat: final answer "Your car is at slot A02,\nDowntown Lot, updated 2 min ago"
    Chat-->>App: chatbot reply
    App-->>Owner: display answer

    Note over Chat,DB: Strict tenant isolation: every tool call re-validates\ntenant_id + owner_user_id before returning data.
    Note over Owner,DB: TARGET-ONLY capability. No chatbot, no LLM\nintegration, no owner-facing "where is my car" API\nexists today (§1) — vehicles link to Employee, not\nowner_user_id, and there is no slot concept to query.
